  "heat": 3,
  "text": "She took Jesus’ own metaphor and flipped it on him… … A Canaanite woman comes after Jesus screaming for help for her demonized daughter. He doesn’t answer her. Not one word. The disciples get annoyed and tell him to send her away because she’s being loud. He says he was only sent to the lost sheep of Israel. She still doesn’t leave. She kneels and says “Lord, help me.” Then he gives her the hard line about not giving the children’s bread to dogs. She doesn’t get offended. She takes his metaphor and flips it: “Truth, Lord… but even the dogs eat the crumbs that fall from the master’s table.” He looks at her and says “O woman, great is thy faith.” Her daughter is healed that hour. She argued with Jesus for crumbs and won. I’m obsessed. ---",
